ysis and financial viability while staying aligned with the company''s goals.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "65801666-8a7c-48ca-a6fb-46fbca77a8df\n0d878ba7-4ece-453d-9b83-e3426d94d1e8", "preferredlabel": "collaborate in the development of marketing strategies"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_1723", "type": "skill", "depth": 3, "label": "plan marketing strategy", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "cdfe83e4-83d0-416b-be7a-2e178c68f3de", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "plan marketing strategy", "altlabels": "plan marketing strategies\narrange marketing strategy\norganise marketing strategy\nplanning a marketing strategy\nplan a marketing strategy\nplan marketing strategy\nproject marketing strategy\ndesign marketing strategy", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/08fd2839-670c-4f16-8024-97437f2035ab", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Determine the objective of the marketing strategy whether it is for establishing image, implementing a pricing strategy, or raising awareness of the product. Establish approaches of marketing actions to ensure that goals are achieved efficiently and over a long term.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "400443a9-a367-4b83-aa47-6094ce0ed5e2\n432ee6b9-cb0e-4f8e-ba1b-c36818af3b8c", "preferredlabel": "plan marketing strategy"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_18148", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_18148", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "cdfe83e4-83d0-416b-be7a-2e178c68f3de", "metadata": {"code": "2511.9", "type": "occupation", "label": "ICT business analyst", "node_id": "occupation::key_18148", "altlabels": "ICT business analyst\nICT business analysts\nbusiness process specialist\nIT business analyst", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/fe0fa514-b48d-4a53-9757-a283c0baacf0", "scopenote": "Excludes people performing development activities.", "definition": "", "description": "ICT business analysts are in charge of analysing and designing an organisation''s processes and systems, assessing the business model and its integration with technology. They also identify change needs, assess the impact of the change, capture and document requirements and then ensure that these requirements are delivered whilst supporting the business through the implementation process.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "f163e862-fee0-4010-a717-6baba039227c\nc84230b4-e268-4567-b54c-f54e53126bdd", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "ICT business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.332122445}, {"id": "occupation::key_17030", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_17030", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": true, "graph_id": "cdfe83e4-83d0-416b-be7a-2e178c68f3de", "metadata": {"code": "2631.2", "type": "occupation", "label": "economist", "node_id": "occupation::key_17030", "altlabels": "macro analyst\neconomics research scientist\neconomics research analyst\nlabour economist\neconometrician\neconomics analyst\neconomist\nsocial economist\neconomics researcher\ninterest analyst\neconomics science researcher\neconophysicist\neconomics scholar\neconomics scientist", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/99492920-e5a5-4dba-9e5a-93193147198c", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Economists perform research and develop theories in the field of economics, whether for microeconomic or macroeconomic analysis. They study trends, analyse statistical data, and to some extent work with economic mathematical models in order to advise companies, governments, and related institutions. They advise on product feasibility, trend forecasts, emerging markets, tax policies, and consumer trends.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "508b30dc-2cbc-4c0d-b66c-e4aa6c44b308\n20539842-7a6e-462d-a544-b9ab4595c46d", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "economist", "occupationgroupcode": "2631", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.384680092}], "anchors": ["skill::key_7226", "skill::key_12645", "skill::key_12039", "skill::key_1648", "skill::key_14407"], "graph_id": "cdfe83e4-83d0-416b-be7a-2e178c68f3de", "tree_type": "enhanced_competence_tree", "anchor_metadata": [{"id": "skill::key_7226", "score": 0.186207, "category": "cognitive", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "apply strategic thinking", "node_id": "skill::key_7226", "altlabels": "apply strategic thinking techniques\napply strategic thinking\napply techniques for strategic thinking\nmove strategically\nthink strategically", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/6c870993-9341-438b-91c0-c7fe4f96d8f5", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Apply generation and effective application of business insights and possible opportunities, in order to achieve competitive business advantage on a long-term basis.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "a71b991a-32ab-4549-be36-4e1937acc883\n964c1d63-681d-4f91-9a0a-0ab87a57fcd8", "preferredlabel": "apply strategic thinking"}, "confidence": 0.85, "esco_label": "Strategic Thinking", "applications": ["Developing business strategies to gain a competitive advantage", "Evaluating market trends and making informed decisions", "Identifying opportunities for organizational growth and sustainability"], "justification": "Given the user''s interest in philosophy, complex environments, and desire to work in a leadership role, strategic thinking aligns with their cognitive strengths and career goals. It involves analyzing situations, understanding connections between various elements, and making decisions that impact others.", "original_label": "Strategic Thinking", "esco_description": "The ability to analyze complex situations, anticipate future trends, and develop long-term plans to achieve organizational goals."}, {"id": "skill::key_12645", "score": 0.306826115, "category": "leadership", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "identify new business opportunities", "node_id": "skill::key_12645", "altlabels": "diagnose new business opportunities\nidentify a new business opportunity\nidentifying new business opportunities\nclassify new business opportunities\nidentifying a new business opportunity\ndetermine new business opportunities\nidentify new business opportunities\nanalyse new business opportunities", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/d207a30b-2f80-4138-9b77-f88d549b8768", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Pursue potential customers or products in order to generate additional sales and ensure growth.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "abdb4e2f-3780-4e3c-bd6d-1282f9d4b531\n184d0ed3-30ec-4414-aa4e-025fc90ecf7c", "preferredlabel": "identify new business opportunities"}, "confidence": 0.8, "esco_label": "Business Development", "applications": ["Identifying new market segments for expansion", "Developing and implementing sales strategies", "Creating and managing business partnerships"], "justification": "The user''s interest in creating companies and building relations between things, coupled with their leadership skills and desire to work in an enterprising environment, makes entrepreneurship a critical anchor skill. It involves taking initiative, understanding market dynamics, and creating val