theories in the field of economics, whether for microeconomic or macroeconomic analysis. They study trends, analyse statistical data, and to some extent work with economic mathematical models in order to advise companies, governments, and related institutions. They advise on product feasibility, trend forecasts, emerging markets, tax policies, and consumer trends.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "508b30dc-2cbc-4c0d-b66c-e4aa6c44b308\n20539842-7a6e-462d-a544-b9ab4595c46d", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "economist", "occupationgroupcode": "2631", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.384680092}, {"id": "occupation::key_18148", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_18148", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": true, "graph_id": "e888249a-e76e-434a-87a5-b44f9f66039a", "metadata": {"code": "2511.9", "type": "occupation", "label": "ICT business analyst", "node_id": "occupation::key_18148", "altlabels": "ICT business analyst\nICT business analysts\nbusiness process specialist\nIT business analyst", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/fe0fa514-b48d-4a53-9757-a283c0baacf0", "scopenote": "Excludes people performing development activities.", "definition": "", "description": "ICT business analysts are in charge of analysing and designing an organisation''s processes and systems, assessing the business model and its integration with technology. They also identify change needs, assess the impact of the change, capture and document requirements and then ensure that these requirements are delivered whilst supporting the business through the implementation process.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "f163e862-fee0-4010-a717-6baba039227c\nc84230b4-e268-4567-b54c-f54e53126bdd", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "ICT business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.332122445}], "anchors": ["skill::key_7226", "skill::key_6843", "skill::key_9267", "skill::key_14407", "skill::key_1648"], "graph_id": "e888249a-e76e-434a-87a5-b44f9f66039a", "tree_type": "enhanced_competence_tree", "anchor_metadata": [{"id": "skill::key_7226", "score": 0.19552379799999997, "category": "cognitive", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "apply strategic thinking", "node_id": "skill::key_7226", "altlabels": "apply strategic thinking techniques\napply strategic thinking\napply techniques for strategic thinking\nmove strategically\nthink strategically", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/6c870993-9341-438b-91c0-c7fe4f96d8f5", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Apply generation and effective application of business insights and possible opportunities, in order to achieve competitive business advantage on a long-term basis.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "a71b991a-32ab-4549-be36-4e1937acc883\n964c1d63-681d-4f91-9a0a-0ab87a57fcd8", "preferredlabel": "apply strategic thinking"}, "confidence": 0.85, "esco_label": "Strategic Thinking", "applications": ["Developing long-term business strategies", "Assessing market trends and competitive landscapes", "Identifying opportunities for organizational growth and development"], "justification": "Given the user''s interest in philosophy and complex environments, strategic thinking aligns with their goal to work in complex environments and their self-identification as a thinker. This skill will build on their existing strengths in critical thinking and analytical thinking, supporting their career trajectory in creating companies and establishing relationships between things.", "original_label": "Strategic Thinking", "esco_description": "The ability to analyze complex situations, identify long-term implications, and develop innovative solutions to achieve organizational goals."}, {"id": "skill::key_6843", "score": 0.271885276, "category": "leadership", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "entrepreneurship", "node_id": "skill::key_6843", "altlabels": "entrepreneurship\nbusiness initiative\nentrepreneurialism", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/658605f2-1c95-49f0-bd98-0af7b15ad0b0", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "The development, organisation and management of an own business venture.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "d5822232-fc8a-48b4-9bf2-a616dbde4bab\na7283b9c-44ac-4d18-849c-d7bba1537276", "preferredlabel": "entrepreneurship"}, "confidence": 0.8, "esco_label": "Entrepreneurship", "applications": ["Developing and implementing business plans", "Seeking and securing funding for new ventures", "Evaluating and managing business risks"], "justification": "As the user aims to help create companies and wants to work in business, entrepreneurship aligns with their career goals. Their leadership skills and desire to inspire others make this skill a solid foundation. It represents an enterprising skill that supports their interest in business and leadership.", "original_label": "Entrepreneurship", "esco_description": "Identifying business opportunities, taking calculated risks, and creating and managing a new venture to achieve success."}, {"id": "skill::key_9267", "score": 0.32856172299999997, "category": "interpersonal", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "influence legislators", "node_id": "skill::key_9267", "altlabels": "pressure law makers\ndominate legislators\ndominate law makers\ncontrol law makers\ncontrol legislators\npressure legislators\ninfluence legislators", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/91fe9c5b-7c12-4835-ad9c-6cae970187fa", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "Influence the organisations and individuals involved in the process of making or changing legislation and laws in order to obtain a desired result, by identifying which parties would be best to contact and using persuasive methods to influence their actions and decisions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "67c90222-9084-4acc-9fde-8168d38c5f71\na6f21ef3-49ec-4e4a-8a37-a36c0cca1beb", "preferredlabel": "influence legislators"}, "confidence": 0.75, "esco_label": "Influencing Others", "applications": ["Negotiating business deals", "Leading and motivating teams", "Advocating for policy changes"], "justification": "The user''s ability to attract attention, make connections, and understand others'' motives indicates a strong interpersonal skill set. Developing interpersonal influence will further enhance their ability to inspire and lead others, aligning with their unique quality and career aspirations.", "original_label": "Interpersonal Influence", "esco_description": "Influencing others involves persuading and convincing individuals or groups to take a specific course of action or adopt a particular belief. It requires effective communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills."}, {"id": "skill::key_14407", "score": 0.35770076500000003, "category": "technical", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "forecast economic trends", "node_id": "skill::key_14407", "altlabels": "project economic trends\neconomic trend forecasting\nforecast economic trends\nanalyse economic trends\npredict economic trends\nforecasting of economic trends\neconomic trend forecasts", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/f2a34d6b-131a-4b8f-a110-898b9c91d18f", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Gather and analyse economic data in order to predict economic trends and events.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "5e187514-cb05-4521-94d0-8f854d9e197b\nbb6b2ce8-10c6-4707-b1b4-1bfb511fffd4", "preferredlabel": "forecast economic trends"}, "confidence": 0.8, "esco_label": "Economic Analysis", "applications": ["Assessing market conditions and forecasting economic trends", "Evaluating the impact of policies and regulations on economic activities", "Providing insights for strategic business planning and investment decisions"], "justification": "Given the user''s education and interest in economics, developing expertise in economic analysis will provide them with a technical skill foundation. This skill aligns with their industry, education, and interest in working with numbers, supporting their career trajectory in economics and business.", "original_label": "Economic Analysis", "esco_description": "Conducting in-depth examination and evaluation of economic data to identify trends, forecast outcomes, and inform decision-making processes in various industries."}, {"id": "skill::key_1648", "score": 0.41281115999999995, "category": "creative", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "propose ICT solutions to business problems", "node_id": "skill::key_1648", "altlabels": "propose technical solutions to business problems\npropose ICT solutions to business problems", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/07e51c60-763a-4335-b4ec-70a15f66d328", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Suggest how to solve business issues, using ICT means, so that business processes are improved.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "57bfedf4-70e2-4736-a01e-ed696a50518a\n2949f643-88a5-411e-83d2-109f0749a45a", "preferredlabel": "propose ICT solutions to business problems"}, "confidence": 0.85, "esco_label": "Problem Solving", "applications": ["Developing new business strategies in the field of economics", "Designing and implementing innovative economic models", "Creating and optimizing financial processes and systems"], "ju