nd the possibilities for change.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "66bbc759-4726-4f84-9951-2951e60e6059\nb7e2137a-2c2d-4d1e-8e68-f04fc6e4a2d1", "preferredlabel": "provide clinical psychological counselling"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_9069", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "apply art therapy interventions", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "apply art therapy interventions", "altlabels": "apply arts therapy interventions\ncarry out arts therapy interventions\nperform arts therapy interventions\napply art therapy interventions\ncarry out art therapy interventions\nperform art therapy interventions", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/8e7e17cf-db69-4191-a856-3a17fe23c5d0", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "Treat individuals or groups in inpatient, outpatient, partial treatment programs, and aftercare with art therapy interventions, to explore verbal, behavioural, and artistic communication, treatment planning, treatment approaches and relationship dynamics.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "aa05edec-03c9-4a00-a28f-c870ed81f148\n6cccbf8d-6542-424d-b4ce-3c4f2811bcb3", "preferredlabel": "apply art therapy interventions"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skillgroup::key_675", "type": "skillgroup", "depth": 2, "label": "psychology", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "", "type": "skillgroup", "label": "psychology", "altlabels": "psychology", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/isced-f/0313", "scopenote": "", "description": "Psychology is the study of the human mind and behaviour as a result of individual differences, experience and environment.\nProgrammes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:\nCognitive science\nPsychoanalysis\nPsychology\nPsychotherapy", "uuidhistory": "a90bb1ca-d453-4005-ab11-6cad5f2aa8ea\nf301fac8-7f28-40c2-86cb-594b47f258db", "preferredlabel": "psychology"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_18098", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "social pedagogue", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "2635.2", "type": "occupation", "label": "social pedagogue", "altlabels": "social pedagogy practitioner\ncommunity educator\nsocial pedagogue\nsocial outreach worker\ncommunity education practitioner\nsocio-cultural animator\npractitioner in social pedagogy\nsocial work pedagogue\ncommunity social pedagogue\nsocial pedagogue cultural animation\nsocial pedagogy project worker\nqualified social pedagogue\ncultural animator\nsocial pedagogy team worker\nsocial educator", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/fa4a3b52-990c-44eb-a912-490f5d689400", "scopenote": "Social pedagogues include in their practice the contributions of family members and other relevant professionals to the task of educating children and young people.", "definition": "", "description": "Social pedagogues provide care, support, and education to children and young persons with different backgrounds or capabilities. They develop educational processes for young persons to be in charge of their own experiences, using a multi-disciplinary approach set to the learning experience. Social pedagogues contribute to the individuals'' learning, welfare, and societal inclusion, and put an emphasis on building self-reliance.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "c7c1155c-2247-45cc-995f-53c7f9552b35\n36084544-7a69-45d8-8d86-c48c2eccf3c8", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "social pedagogue", "occupationgroupcode": "2635", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_11578", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "support patients to understand their conditions", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "support patients to understand their conditions", "altlabels": "aid the psychological development of the healthcare user\nhelp patients to understand and manage their conditions\nsupport patients to understand and manage their conditions\nfacilitate the psychological development of the healthcare user\nsupport the process of patient self-discovery about their condition\naid the psychological development of the patient\nhelp patients to understand their conditions\nfoster the psychological development of the patient\nfacilitate the psychological development of the patient\nfoster the psychological development of the healthcare user\nsupport patients to understand their conditions", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/beb7712f-5a8a-4a4d-b75c-e3165a3da7cd", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "Facilitate the process of self-discovery for the healthcare user, helping them to learn about their condition and become more aware of and in control of moods, feelings, thoughts, behaviour, and their origins. Help the healthcare user learn to manage problems and difficulties with greater resilience.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "a83858f9-e1e1-4060-9661-872b178e70c3\n8ca1f0b9-27b3-43d1-b74d-b635b3ebed90", "preferredlabel": "support patients to understand their conditions"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_8272", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "handle patient trauma", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "handle patient trauma", "altlabels": "address traumatised patients\nsupport traumatised patients\nmake assessments of traumatised patients\ndeal with patient trauma\nsupport patients affected by trauma\nhandle traumatised patients\ndeal with traumatised patients\nmake assessments of patient trauma\naddress patient trauma\nperform assessments of patient trauma\nhandle trauma\nhandle patient trauma", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/7fd3b5e4-8f7c-461c-8faa-203cf4b2b0fc", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "Assess the competences, needs, and limitations of people affected by trauma, referring the patients to specialised trauma services where appropriate.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "4d00f62d-f65e-4424-ada6-32e36437cbe3\na35f5dd0-4580-4b9a-afe3-114e15a4b672", "preferredlabel": "handle patient trauma"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_4243", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "work with healthcare users under medication", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "work with healthcare users under medication", "altlabels": "work with health care users on medication\nwork with healthcare users under medication\nwork with patients using prescribed medications\nwork with service users under medication\nwork with health care users under medication\nwork with service users on medication\nwork with a healthcare user under medication\nwork with healthcare users on medication", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/35f1f02e-f1b9-44a2-92d3-032