hologist\nhealth psychology researcher\nexpert healthcare psychologist\nconsultant in health psychology\nhealthcare psychologist\nhealth psychologist\npractitioner of healthcare psychology\nresearch health psychologist\nconsultant health psychologist", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/976c7f50-7f9e-4347-bbb9-f0dc842046a3", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Health psychologists deal with the various aspects of health related behaviour of individuals and groups, by helping individuals or groups prevent illness and promote healthy behaviours by also providing counseling services. They perform tasks for the development of health promotion activities and projects on the basis of psychological science, research findings, theories, methods and techniques. They also engage in research about health related issues to influence public policy on health care issues.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "76e30b2f-8dfe-4619-99b5-25f51c6da4e1\n962533a5-0842-4c39-b811-f9f3059a924f", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "health psychologist", "occupationgroupcode": "2634", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_9858", "type": "skill", "depth": 3, "label": "adolescent psychological development", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "adolescent psychological development", "altlabels": "adolescent psychological development\nadolescents'' psychological development\nadolescent''s psychological development\npsychological development of adolescents\nadolescent behavioural development\npsychological development of an adolescent\npsychological development of children and young persons", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/9ccecb58-e720-4465-b309-46e362ca6f75", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Understand the developments and the development needs of children and young persons, observing the behaviour and the attachment relationships in order to detect developmental delay.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "0a86571c-c0c6-4abd-8e05-d53576c9e95f\ndd663b7b-3b51-4b50-901b-1085f318f985", "preferredlabel": "adolescent psychological development"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16397", "type": "occupation", "depth": 3, "label": "emergency ambulance driver", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "3258.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "emergency ambulance driver", "altlabels": "technician in emergency medical care\nambulance emergency medical technician\nassistant in emergency care\nambulance technician\nECA\nemergency medical vehicle assistant\nmedical emergency assistant\nambulance emergency care assistant\nemergency ambulance driver", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/64e909ad-1bd0-493c-a8dc-1afbed0c9c2f", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Emergency ambulance drivers use emergency vehicles to respond to medical emergencies and support the work of paramedics, move patients safely, take note of changes in the patient''s vital signs and report to the paramedics in charge, ensuring the medical equipment is well stored, transported and functional, under supervision and on order of a doctor of medicine.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "6daf9b43-1c92-4262-8104-2ef74bda16f9\nb69edaf7-0f74-4d6b-b9e8-174412bcfd79", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "emergency ambulance driver", "occupationgroupcode": "3258", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_17887", "type": "occupation", "depth": 3, "label": "animal assisted therapist", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "2269.9.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "animal assisted therapist", "altlabels": "animal assisted intervention professional\nanimal assisted therapist", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/e6023abf-ced3-4ac9-9437-cc79e4396e3e", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Animal assisted therapists provide support to individuals with cognitive, motoric, or social-emotional disabilities through animal assisted intervention. They involve pets and domesticated animals in a specific intervention plan such as therapy, education, and human service, and aim to restore and maintain the patients` well-being and recovery.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "7ccde7de-00bc-4226-94b1-f6eae7270c6a\n53b22634-8d16-40e1-887f-ada46eb73c20", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "animal assisted therapist", "occupationgroupcode": "2269", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_17269", "type": "occupation", "depth": 3, "label": "psychotherapist", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "2634.2.4", "type": "occupation", "label": "psychotherapist", "altlabels": "geriatric psychotherapist\nhypno-psychotherapist\npsychotherapist\nspecialist psychotherapist\nperson-centered psychotherapist\nperson-centred psychotherapist\nbody psychotherapist\npositive psychotherapist\nneuro-linguistic psychotherapist\ntransactional analytic psychotherapist\ngestalt psychotherapist\nexpert psychotherapist\nexpert in psychotherapy\npsycoterapy expert\nchild psychotherapist\nintegrative psychotherapist\npsychoanalytical psychotherapist\ncognitive behavioural therapist\nsystemic therapist\npractitioner of psychotherapy\nhumanistic psychotherapist\npsychotherapy practitioner\nmulti-modal psychotherapist\ngroup psychotherapist\npsychodrama psychotherapist\ntranspersonal psychotherapist\npsychodynamic psychotherapist\nyouth psychotherapist\nreality therapy psychotherapist\nexistential psychotherapist", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/af69484e-b43f-4685-b22d-f3418df45c4d", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Psychotherapists assist and treat healthcare users with varying degrees of psychological, psychosocial, or psychosomatic behavioural disorders and pathogenic conditions by means of psychotherapeutic methods. They promote personal development and well-being and provide advice on improving relationships, capabilities, and problem-solving techniques. They use science-based psychotherapeutic methods such as behavioural therapy, existential analysis and logotherapy, psychoanalysis or systemic family therapy in order to guide the patients in their development and help them search for appropriate solutions to their problems. Psychotherapists are not required to have academic degrees in psychology or a medical qualification in psychiatry. It is an independent occupation from psychology, psychiatry, and counselling.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "daefd51c-345e-4d4f-afaf-2de316bc85dd\nfa178cd5-3562-4b9e-9b54-be05200e5e9f", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "psychotherapist", "occupationgroupcode": "2634", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skillgroup::key_1085", "type": "skillgroup", "depth": 3, "label": "working with others", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "S1.8.0", "type": "skillgroup", "label": "working with others", "altlabels": "working with others", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/91b0b918-942e-4661-b88c-70b9396529e5", "scopenote": "Excludes:\n- Management, supervision and coordination of teams", "description": "Working with other people, understanding and respecting the roles and competencies of others.", "uuidhistory": "6e8910b2-83d3-4234-9c21-db71dfb64c48\n674adf11-2643-4e98-ab18-b52b69476b50", "preferredlabel": "working with others"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_17472", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_17472", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "5221.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "retail entrepreneur", "node_id": "occupation::key_17472", "altlabels": "retail business developer\nretail business entrepreneur\nshop keeper\nretail trade entrepreneur\nretail product developer\nretailer\nretail business transformer\nshopping entrepreneur\nretail innovator\nretail experience entrepreneur\nretail entrepreneur\nentrepreneur\nretail sales entrepreneur", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/bf89925d-00a1-4f94-ab3b-2148c887af33", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Retail entrepreneurs organise business processes and concepts in his/her personally owned business.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "3f326240-d06b-452f-ae09-f12a61c7e562\n6709322a-e8f4-4e67-b070-5e436fdd6544", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "retail entrepreneur", "occupationgroupcode": "5221", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.386391759}, {"id": "occupation::key_16339", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_16339", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "2421.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "business analyst", "node_id": "occupation::key_16339", "altlabels": "business analyst\nstandardisation manager\nmanagement consultant\norganisational developer\nbusiness strategy consultant\nbusiness development analyst\nstandardisation expert\nbusiness strategy analyst\nstandardization expert", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/60082a99-d8ef-4e84-9290-78902681b6ed", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "\nBusiness analysts research and understand the strategic position of businesses and companies in relation to their markets and their stakeholders. They analyse and present their views on how the company, from many perspectives, can improve its strategic position and internal corporate structure. They assess needs for change, communication methods, technology, IT tools, new standards and certifications.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "75ccaf1d-6a97-41ad-a3ae-e2944c2b90cf\n5dd8d5bc-e7f6-4471-ab7c-237d30458e7a", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2421", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.35966897}, {"id": "occupation::key_18148", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "occupation::key_18148", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": true, "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "metadata": {"code": "2511.9", "type": "occupation", "label": "ICT business analyst", "node_id": "occupation::key_18148", "altlabels": "ICT business analyst\nICT business analysts\nbusiness process specialist\nIT business analyst", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/fe0fa514-b48d-4a53-9757-a283c0baacf0", "scopenote": "Excludes people performing development activities.", "definition": "", "description": "ICT business analysts are in charge of analysing and designing an organisation''s processes and systems, assessing the business model and its integration with technology. They also identify change needs, assess the impact of the change, capture and document requirements and then ensure that these requirements are delivered whilst supporting the business through the implementation process.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "f163e862-fee0-4010-a717-6baba039227c\nc84230b4-e268-4567-b54c-f54e53126bdd", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "ICT business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 0, "similarity_score": 0.332122445}], "anchors": ["skill::key_6843", "skill::key_9435", "skill::key_8161", "skill::key_14598", "skill::key_1648"], "graph_id": "16b67717-a56b-48e2-ba7e-a855dee748d0", "tree_type": "enhanced_competence_tree", "anchor_metadata": [{"id": "skill::key_6843", "score": 0.23768478599999998, "category": "leadership", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "entrepreneurship", "node_id": "skill::key_6843", "altlabels": "entrepreneurship\nbusiness initiative\nentrepreneurialism", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/658605f2-1c95-49f0-bd98-0af7b15ad0b0", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "The development, organisation and management of an own business venture.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "d5822232-fc8a-48b4-9bf2-a616dbde4bab\na7283b9c-44ac-4d18-849c-d7bba1537276", "preferredlabel": "entrepreneurship"}, "confidence": 0.85, "esco_label": "Entrepreneurship", "applications": ["Developing business plans and strategies", "Seeking funding and investment opportunities", "Managing business operations and growth"], "justification": "Given the user''s interest in creating companies and their strong leadership and enterprising traits, developing entrepreneurship skills will align with their career goals and enable them to work in complex environments while utilizing their leadership abilities.", "original_label": "Entrepreneurship", "esco_description": "Identifying business opportunities, taking calculated risks, and managing resources to create and develop new ventures."}, {"id": "skill::key_9435", "score": 0.463670433, "category": "interpersonal", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "interpret psychological tests", "node_id": "skill::key_9435", "altlabels": "obtain information from psychological test\ninterpret psychological test\nobtain information from psychological tests\nanalyze psychological tests\ninterpret psychological tests\nanalyse psychological tests", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/94f2935b-b4ac-446e-9775-60b4239d016c", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Interpret psychological tests in order to obtain information on patients'' intelligence, achievements, interests, and personality.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "a1ceeb09-8d8c-4f34-97ba-70450ba23f75\n6faf7c00-4b49-494b-991d-da44c5208227", "preferredlabel": "interpret psychological tests"}, "confidence": 0.8, "esco_label": "Psychological Analysis", "applications": ["Conducting psychological assessments for economic decision-making", "Applying psychological insights to consumer behavior analysis", "Utilizing psychological understanding to inform economic policy development"], "justification": "With a keen interest in understanding people, the user would benefit from developing skills in psychology to enhance their ability to create relations between things and work in complex environments requiring an understanding of people.", "original_label": "Psychological Understanding", "esco_description": "Utilizing psychological understanding to analyze human behavior, emotions, and thought processes in professional contexts."}, {"id": "skill::key_8161", "score": 0.345473766, "category": "cognitive", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "think critically", "node_id": "skill::key_8161", "altlabels": "weigh information\nassess information\ncheck facts\nevaluate important information\nevaluating information\ndetect bias\nevaluate opinions\nconsider alternative views\nassess facts\nassess opinions\nevaluate information and its sources\nevaluate information\ndistinguish fact from opinion\nevaluate truth\nassess processes\nverify information\ncritically evaluate information and its sources\nevaluate facts\nreview information\napply critical thinking\nthink critically", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/7dd94ad3-13d6-43fe-8b94-51fcbf67ced9", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "transversal", "description": "Make and defend judgements based on internal evidence and external criteria. Critically evaluate the credibility and reliability of information before using or passing it on to others. Develop independent and critical thinking.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "b49909ff-d5a7-4485-ba38-51806d8f3841\n9cedb574-55f2-4e23-b3fe-3180a0c22259", "preferredlabel": "think critically"}, "confidence": 0.9, "esco_label": "Critical Thinking", "applications": ["Analyzing economic data to identify trends and patterns", "Evaluating the impact of policy changes on economic indicators", "Formulating evidence-based recommendations for economic strategies"], "justification": "Building on the user''s existing strength in critical thinking, further developing this skill will support their goal of working in complex environments, as it is essential for analyzing and solving complex problems, which is aligned with their career interests in investigative and enterprising fields.", "original_label": "Critical Thinking", "esco_description": "Analyzing and evaluating information to make reasoned judgments and decisions. It involves logical reasoning, problem-solving, and the ability to think systematically."}, {"id": "skill::key_14598", "score": 0.22185272, "category": "leadership", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "make strategic business decisions", "node_id": "skill::key_14598", "altlabels": "make tactical business decisions\npay per click\nmake strategic business decisions\nmake strategic business choices\nPPC", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/f60c9e52-95fc-4ca1-a73c-18a491153b63", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Analyse business information and consult directors for decision making purposes in a varied array of aspects affecting the prospect, productivity and sustainable operation of a company. Consider the options and alternatives to a challenge and make sound rational decisions based on analysis and experience.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "71709697-2eda-4fe4-9160-e6a258ea6b0a\n0441380e-ef76-4ac6-b610-8c854edf11df", "preferredlabel": "make strategic business decisions"}, "confidence": 0.85, "esco_label": "Strategic Decision Making", "applications": ["Developing long-term business strategies", "Evaluating investment opportunities", "Assessing market trends and competitive landscapes"], "justification": "With a desire to help create companies and a strong interest in leadership and entrepreneurial endeavors, developing skills in strategic decision making will support the user in making impactful decisions and leading others in the business context.", "original_label": "Strategic Decision Making", "esco_description": "The ability to analyze complex situations, consider various options, and make informed decisions that align with organizational goals and objectives."}, {"id": "skill::key_1648", "score": 0.388953, "category": "creative", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "propose ICT solutions to business problems", "node_id": "skill::key_1648", "altlabels": "propose technical solutions to business problems\npropose ICT solutions to business problems", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/07e51c60-763a-4335-b4ec-70a15f66d328", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Suggest how to solve business issues, using ICT means, so that business processes are improved.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "57bfedf4-70e2-4736-a01e-ed696a50518a\n2949f643-88a5-411e-83d2-109f0749a45a", "preferredlabel": "propose ICT solutions to business problems"}, "confidence": 0.8, "esco_label": "Problem Solving", "applications": ["Developing new business models in the economics industry", "Designing and implementing cost-saving measures", "Creating innovative strategies to address economic challenges"], "justification": "Given the user''s high creativity rating and interest in working in complex environments, developing creative problem-solving skills will enable them to apply their creativity to solve complex business and interpersonal challenges, aligning with their career goals and personal strengths.", "original_label": "Creative Problem Solving", "esco_description": "The ability to creatively analyze complex issues, identify innovative solutions, and implement effective problem-solving strategies."}], "generation_method": "graph_traversal"}', '2025-06-10 08:30:32.464735');
