 making adjustments along the way. Evaluate the extent to which strategic objectives have been achieved, learn lessons, celebrate success and recognise people’s contributions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "3bb06545-dcb9-4a3a-8d1e-0e903cd3c03e\n066d8a79-133c-4c05-9998-fb05902d598f", "preferredlabel": "implement operational business plans"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_15769", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "financial manager", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "423de973-5e42-42e1-a7fd-bd0f1035f429", "metadata": {"code": "1211.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "financial manager", "altlabels": "corporate finance manager\nfinancial administrator\nCFO\nchief financial officer\nfinance chief\nfinancial manager\nfinancial director\nfinance manager", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/30f3ea93-882a-4525-841c-1d5b4b64076f", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Financial managers handle all the matters in reference to the finance and investments of a company. They manage financial operations of companies such as the assets, liabilities, equity and cash flow aiming to maintain the financial health of the company and operative viability. Financial managers evaluate the strategic plans of the company in financial terms, maintain transparent financial operations for taxation and auditing bodies, and create the financial statements of the company at the end of the fiscal year.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "50abb007-8705-4c25-a5a5-0d9bf1b20cc4\n2aa51a19-0e23-4c1d-8257-246ad70d2ac3", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "financial manager", "occupationgroupcode": "1211", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation: