es, take calculated risks, and drive innovation in business and economic contexts. It involves a proactive approach to problem-solving and a willingness to adapt to changing market conditions."}, {"id": "skill::key_9267", "score": 0.347289383, "category": "interpersonal", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "influence legislators", "node_id": "skill::key_9267", "altlabels": "pressure law makers\ndominate legislators\ndominate law makers\ncontrol law makers\ncontrol legislators\npressure legislators\ninfluence legislators", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/91fe9c5b-7c12-4835-ad9c-6cae970187fa", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "Influence the organisations and individuals involved in the process of making or changing legislation and laws in order to obtain a desired result, by identifying which parties would be best to contact and using persuasive methods to influence their actions and decisions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "67c90222-9084-4acc-9fde-8168d38c5f71\na6f21ef3-49ec-4e4a-8a37-a36c0cca1beb", "preferredlabel": "influence legislators"}, "confidence": 0.75, "esco_label": "Influencing Others", "applications": ["Negotiating business deals", "Building consensus in team settings", "Persuading stakeholders to support a proposal"], "justification": "Based on the user''s ability to attract attention and make connections, improving interpersonal influence skills would enhance their ability to inspire others and build meaningful relationships in complex environments.", "original_label": "Interpersonal Influence", "esco_description": "Influencing others involves persuading and convincing individuals or groups to adopt a certain course of action or mindset. It requires effective communication, negotiation, and the ability to build rapport and trust."}, {"id": "skill::key_5129", "score": 0.37911987300000005, "category": "technical", "metadata": {"type": "skill", 