tance, security, leisure, competition, transportation, obedience and routine handling, entertainment and education, in accordance with national legislation.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "83023fe2-f1c1-42a7-81a1-bd92eb9f693a\nef7f44fb-66b3-422a-9b91-ec72ecb84cc9", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "animal trainer", "occupationgroupcode": "5164", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_15729", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "animal welfare inspector", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "8143df11-a044-474d-8305-883999879f3c", "metadata": {"code": "5419.9", "type": "occupation", "label": "animal welfare inspector", "altlabels": "animal social worker\nanimal welfare worker\nanimal welfare officer\nanimal control officer\nanimal welfare inspectors\nanimal rescue inspector\nanimal welfare coordinator\nanimal protection officer\nanimal rescue operator\nanimal welfare inspector\nanimal wellbeing officer", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/2de007c6-3223-4cd1-9561-e8a2e16e049d", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": " Animal welfare inspectors investigate alleged reports of animal cruelty or neglect, rescue or collect animals in immediate or potential risk, liaise with internal and external agencies and other animal welfare establishments, educate and advise owners and carers of animals, seek to improve or maintain the welfare of the animal(s), and prevent or alleviate suffering. \n", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "3eb89bb8-e9a7-4e98-9fee-127b2fc97b4d\n550ce0cb-82e5-4725-89b8-c2d67f79c5de", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "animal welfare inspector", "occupationgroupcode": "5419", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revea