work design and administration is the study of the design, maintenance and integration of software applications. Computer media applications are included.\nProgrammes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:\nComputer administration and management\nComputer media applications\nComputer network installation and maintenance\nDatabase administrator studies\nInformation technology administration\nInformation technology security\nNetwork administration\nNetwork design\nWeb design", "uuidhistory": "25337593-578d-451a-9646-dea8c3db3f21\n97dd58e5-c52c-44b0-9376-896f63122d21", "preferredlabel": "database and network design and administration"}, "revealed": false, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16650", "type": "occupation", "depth": 1, "label": "blockchain architect", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "2511.14.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "blockchain architect", "altlabels": "decentralized ledger technology specialist\nblockchain technology specialist\nblockchain engineer\nDLT specialist\nblockchain architect", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/78faf623-2543-43a5-acb2-3c43a22d36e4", "scopenote": "Excludes the development of decentralized systems.", "definition": "", "description": "Blockchain architects are ICT system architects that are specialized in blockchain-based solutions. They design architecture, components, modules, interfaces, and data for a decentralized system to meet specified requirements.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "1faddd14-b23d-4dd8-b0fe-83449384d1d3\n52e5d392-6199-43c8-abb3-772745472fbb", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "blockchain architect", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_17237", "type": "occupation", "depth": 1, "label": "power distribution engineer", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "2151.1.5", "type": "occupation", "label": "power distribution engineer", "altlabels": "power distribution technology engineering specialist\npower distribution engineering expert\npower distribution engineering adviser\npower distribution engineer\npower distribution engineering specialist\npower distribution technology engineering consultant\npower distribution systems engineer\npower distribution system engineer\npower distribution technology engineering adviser\npower distribution technology engineering expert\npower distribution technology engineer\npower distributions engineer\npower distribution engineering consultant", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/ac37627c-a999-4779-997e-9795cc4f9a3d", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Power distribution engineers design and operate facilities which distribute power from the distribution facility to the consumers. They research methods for the optimisation of power distribution, and ensure the consumers'' needs are met. They also ensure compliance to safety regulations by monitoring the automated processes in plants and directing workflow.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "1aec8d79-59a0-4a7f-8479-c2bc6e363e57\n34c0cd53-096e-4802-b112-bdbfa69c9a05", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "power distribution engineer", "occupationgroupcode": "2151", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16339", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "business analyst", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "2421.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "business analyst", "altlabels": "business analyst\nstandardisation manager\nmanagement consultant\norganisational developer\nbusiness strategy consultant\nbusiness development analyst\nstandardisation expert\nbusiness strategy analyst\nstandardization expert", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/60082a99-d8ef-4e84-9290-78902681b6ed", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "\nBusiness analysts research and understand the strategic position of businesses and companies in relation to their markets and their stakeholders. They analyse and present their views on how the company, from many perspectives, can improve its strategic position and internal corporate structure. They assess needs for change, communication methods, technology, IT tools, new standards and certifications.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "75ccaf1d-6a97-41ad-a3ae-e2944c2b90cf\n5dd8d5bc-e7f6-4471-ab7c-237d30458e7a", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2421", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16460", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "business consultant", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "2421.2", "type": "occupation", "label": "business consultant", "altlabels": "business consultant\nbusiness process consultant", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/6a29d804-f775-446c-bec7-35fc4e28ac97", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Business consultants analyse the position, structure and processes of businesses and companies and offer services or advice to improve them. They research and identify business processes such as financial inefficiencies or employee management and devise strategical plans to overcome these difficulties. They work in external consulting firms where they provide an objective view on a business and or company''s structure and methodological processes.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "3e3a36bc-199a-4fb9-a3fa-cf27cd12f9d0\n40a08cf1-51ab-41e4-b917-aead4c203dc0", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "business consultant", "occupationgroupcode": "2421", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_11512", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "business strategy concepts", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "business strategy concepts", "altlabels": "business strategy concepts", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/bd698bbe-7003-4508-b422-46c2ff4d5e95", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "The terminology related to the design and implementation of major trends and aims which are taken by an organisation''s executives, while keeping in mind its resources, competition and environments.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "ee42d3fa-ba4a-427a-bf1f-abbceddcfc98\neceb5ffc-f8c7-45b7-a6c3-b61223c9b66a", "preferredlabel": "business strategy concepts"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skillgroup::key_1020", "type": "skillgroup", "depth": 2, "label": "developing objectives and strategies", "notes": "", "state": "locked", "visible": false, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "S4.1", "type": "skillgroup", "label": "developing objectives and strategies", "altlabels": "str