iate and impactful procedure in order to reach the organisation''s objectives and ensure genuine competition. Define element such as features, scope and duration of the procedure, division into lots, techniques and instruments for electronic submission and types of contract and contract performance clauses.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "e83f4a44-5024-4173-9368-e836ff01098c\ndeb70c82-3220-40a7-8ca0-c83ea1ff129d", "preferredlabel": "develop procurement strategy"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16476", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "chief executive officer", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "f4557296-1cde-4d76-8c6f-9e56b2516ddb", "metadata": {"code": "1120.3", "type": "occupation", "label": "chief executive officer", "altlabels": "managing director\nsenior executive officer\nCEO\nchief executive officer\npresident\nchairman", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/6c3fd65e-2d24-47d8-bc22-9e93512bdcc2", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Chief executive officers hold the highest ranking in a pyramidal corporate structure. They are able to hold a complete idea of the functioning of the business, its departments, risks, and stakeholders. They analyse different kinds of information and create links among them for decision-making purposes. They serve as a  communication link with the board of directors for reporting and implementation of the overall strategy.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "c9b0ed99-513c-4b95-b129-7c05bc5b37d6\need36ec6-490d-4ba3-a58e-7d92135fb679", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "chief executive officer", "occupationgroupcode": "1120", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_1755