nalysis\nfiscal audit\nfiscal analysis", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/99571e68-801f-49af-a897-5f75996642e1", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "The process of assessing the financial possibilities, means, and status of an organisation or individual by analysing financial statements and reports in order to make well informed business or financial decisions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "51bd907f-16b1-4853-aede-fc367cc2cbb8\nad156d42-4499-4d0a-8a6d-09fa1aa05165", "preferredlabel": "financial analysis"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skillgroup::key_1195", "type": "skillgroup", "depth": 1, "label": "analysing financial and economic data", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "S2.7.3", "type": "skillgroup", "label": "analysing financial and economic data", "altlabels": "analysing financial and economic data", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/d94e1143-3a3a-4f6a-a881-df93bf56cf23", "scopenote": "Excludes:\n- Risk analysis\n- Using ICT tools to analyse and process data.\n\nExamples:\n- Forecast economic trends\n- Prepare financial projections\n- Consult credit scores", "description": "Analysing and evaluating information and data on finances and on economic and market trends.", "uuidhistory": "5b97c59f-e8fd-4c77-bce9-78570968bb4c\n5ea7fb86-e2e7-4cd1-a4c6-95770db8cebd", "preferredlabel": "analysing financial and economic data"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_2782", "type": "skill", "depth": 1, "label": "pricing strategies", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "pricing strategies", "altlabels": "pricing strategies\npricing strategy\npricing plans\nprice strategies\npricing tactics", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/1c460d2d-90c6-4fc9-ad49-febb6e15605a", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "The techniques, theories, and commonly accepted strategies regarding pricing of goods. The relation between pricing strategies and outcomes in the market such as profitability maximisation, deterrence of newcomers, or increase of market share.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "aee5c88f-cc76-4aa6-abca-4111767ea92c\nb011685d-5016-4dd1-a892-eea252e0053f", "preferredlabel": "pricing strategies"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_18148", "type": "occupation", "depth": 1, "label": "ICT business analyst", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "2511.9", "type": "occupation", "label": "ICT business analyst", "altlabels": "ICT business analyst\nICT business analysts\nbusiness process specialist\nIT business analyst", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/fe0fa514-b48d-4a53-9757-a283c0baacf0", "scopenote": "Excludes people performing development activities.", "definition": "", "description": "ICT business analysts are in charge of analysing and designing an organisation''s processes and systems, assessing the business model and its integration with technology. They also identify change needs, assess the impact of the change, capture and document requirements and then ensure that these requirements are delivered whilst supporting the business through the implementation process.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "f163e862-fee0-4010-a717-6baba039227c\nc84230b4-e268-4567-b54c-f54e53126bdd", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "ICT business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_12389", "type": "skill", "depth": 1, "label": "business ICT systems", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "business ICT systems", "altlabels": "business IT systems\nbusiness ICT systems", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/ccdbd9bb-4faf-403c-a968-e8bf487f8a53", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "knowledge", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "sector-specific", "description": "The software packages, hardware devices and new technologies used in supporting business processes such as enterprise resource planning (ERP), customer relationship management (CRM), mobile devices and network solutions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "69e2b00e-c93a-4ca8-a3cb-8867f322a233\n58f3f5b1-9c5d-4de3-b3c5-b0a36b1341e7", "preferredlabel": "business ICT systems"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16074", "type": "occupation", "depth": 1, "label": "ICT business analysis manager", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "2511.8", "type": "occupation", "label": "ICT business analysis manager", "altlabels": "IT business analysis director\nIT business analysis manager\nIT commercial analysis manager\nlead IT business analyst\nICT business analysis managers\nICT commercial analysis manager\nICT business analysis manager", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/4b3201cb-ffc5-4f61-9fc3-5c0f0038fa5f", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "ICT business analysis managers identify areas where information system changes are needed to support business plans and monitor the impact in terms of change management. They contribute to the general ICT functional requirements of the business organisation. ICT business analysis managers analyse business needs and translate them into ICT solutions.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "62539696-8d8a-4027-91b9-2729867a7356\ndb71c6d9-248a-42ec-8656-4efabaa243ba", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "ICT business analysis manager", "occupationgroupcode": "2511", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_16339", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "business analyst", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "2421.1", "type": "occupation", "label": "business analyst", "altlabels": "business analyst\nstandardisation manager\nmanagement consultant\norganisational developer\nbusiness strategy consultant\nbusiness development analyst\nstandardisation expert\nbusiness strategy analyst\nstandardization expert", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/60082a99-d8ef-4e84-9290-78902681b6ed", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "\nBusiness analysts research and understand the strategic position of businesses and companies in relation to their markets and their stakeholders. They analyse and present their views on how the company, from many perspectives, can improve its strategic position and internal corporate structure. They assess needs for change, communication methods, technology, IT tools, new standards and certifications.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "75ccaf1d-6a97-41ad-a3ae-e2944c2b90cf\n5dd8d5bc-e7f6-4471-ab7c-237d30458e7a", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "business analyst", "occupationgroupcode": "2421", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregul