onal communication", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "promote organisational communication", "altlabels": "encourage creative processes\nfoster organisational communication\npromote communication within organisation\npromoting organisational communication\npromote organizational  communication\ninspire organisational communication\npromote organisational communication", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/656b2dab-4ace-4afa-bad4-d9ddef577e2b", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Promote and nurture the efficient spread of plans and business information throughout the organisation by strengthening the channels of communication at its disposal.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "e2707f22-bf8b-427b-8311-f749c9daed78\n0f1f2ba6-beb7-41f6-9e16-7fe2df7e65d1", "preferredlabel": "promote organisational communication"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_8847", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "analyse financial performance of a company", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "analyse financial performance of a company", "altlabels": "examine financial performance of a company\nanalyze  financial performance of a company\ninvestigate financial performance of a company\nevaluate financial performance of a company\nanalysing financial performance of company\nanalyse company financial performance\nanalyse financial performance of companies\nreview financial performance of a company\nstudy financial performance of a company\nanalyse financial performance of a company", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/skill/8a43795b-bb38-4f29-91df-a6c92ad4643c", "scopenote": "", "skilltype": "skill/competence", "definition": "", "reuselevel": "cross-sector", "description": "Analyse the performance of the company in financial matters in order to identify improvement actions that could increase profit, based on accounts, records, financial statements and external information of the market.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "c6f1923a-5d48-43ad-96c4-b9c971dde5e5\nbccc5ad7-099e-4521-b283-9ac295c7d9a2", "preferredlabel": "analyse financial performance of a company"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skillgroup::key_693", "type": "skillgroup", "depth": 2, "label": "finance, banking and insurance", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "", "type": "skillgroup", "label": "finance, banking and insurance", "altlabels": "finance, banking and insurance", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/isced-f/0412", "scopenote": "", "description": "Finance, banking and insurance is the study of planning, directing, organizing and controlling financial activities and services. It includes the control and monitoring of the financial resources of organizations, institutions and individuals, and the provision of financial services at the corporate and individual level.\nProgrammes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:\nBank teller studies\nBanking and finance\nFinance theory\nInsurance\nInvestment analysis\nInvestments and securities\nPension insurance\nSocial insurance\nStock-broking\n\n=== Exclusions\nStudy of actuarial science is excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0542 ''Statistics''.", "uuidhistory": "568f6269-b544-495a-9bca-b175f80a053b\nf4d8c0c9-14f6-42c7-a80c-51730aa38691", "preferredlabel": "finance, banking and insurance"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "occupation::key_15491", "type": "occupation", "depth": 2, "label": "financial auditor", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"code": "2411.1.7", "type": "occupation", "label": "financial auditor", "altlabels": "financial auditor\ninternal auditor\nbank auditor\nauditor\ninternal examiner\nfinance auditor\naudit manager\nfinances auditor\nsenior internal auditor\nchartered accountant\nfinancial examiner\nexternal auditor\nbank examiner\nexternal examiner\nfinancial systems analyst", "originuri": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/occupation/1ad59946-d13e-441e-9b36-56e1df055e21", "scopenote": "", "definition": "", "description": "Financial auditors collect and examine financial data for clients, organisations and companies. They ensure the financial data is properly maintained and free of material misstatements due to error or fraud, that it adds up, and functions legally and effectively. They review lending and credit policies or numbers in databases and documents, evaluate, consult and assist the source of the transaction if necessary. They use their review of the client''s financial governance as assurance to give testimony to the shareholders, stakeholders and board of directors of the organisation or company that all is up to par.", "islocalized": "false", "uuidhistory": "47c9ad5f-d5b8-4a82-88b8-5ffe00052c36\n06510ba9-5abc-43a2-b571-aec2a5db200e", "occupationtype": "escooccupation", "preferredlabel": "financial auditor", "occupationgroupcode": "2411", "regulatedprofessionnote": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/regulated-professions/unregulated"}, "revealed": true, "challenge": "", "is_anchor": false, "xp_reward": 25, "similarity_score": 0.5}, {"id": "skill::key_6479", "type": "skill", "depth": 2, "label": "analyse economic trends", "notes": "", "state": "available", "visible": true, "graph_id": "7bcdafac-17ac-4177-9ff0-f9a285d55b56", "metadata": {"type": "skill", "label": "analyse economic trends", "altlabels": "i